    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:d1bf136a4a3c936a",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "eb72f15526f582ee0cdefee97d0c98645c665b049bf1db1d4a95dede0926a864",
      "text": "After breakfast, set out on a tour of the city and island. The first part of the tour takes you through 15 November Square, one of the main historic squares in Florianópolis.\n\nThe square is home to the Cruz e Sousa Palace, which hosted important events, including receptions for Brazilian emperors. It now houses the Santa Catarina History Museum.\n\nNext, stop at the Hercílio Luz Bridge, the first bridge built in the city to link Santa Catarina Island to the mainland.\n\nContinue to Lagoa da Conceição, a favourite spot with locals. The water is calm, and historic houses survive around the lagoon.\n\nReturn to your hotel after the tour.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw62hj6e-l11w8-amanda",
        "model": "ChatGPT",
        "wordAbsenceReason": "The Day 11 Word paragraph lists the bridge, historic centre and lagoon but omits 15 November Square, the palace and museum, and the return to the hotel. It also lists beaches absent from the current RU city-tour block, so there is no complete equivalent passage."
      }
    },
